      "text": "The given equation of the hyperbola is \\(\\frac{x^2}{99} - \\frac{y^2}{36} = 1\\). This is a standard form of a hyperbola that opens left and right, where \\(a^2 = 99\\) and \\(b^2 = 36\\). The distance between the vertices of a hyperbola is given by \\(2a\\).\n\nFirst, we identify the value of \\(a\\):\n\\[a^2 = 99 \\implies a = \\sqrt{99} = 3\\sqrt{11}.\\]\nThus, the distance between the vertices is:\n\\[2a = 2 \\times 3\\sqrt{11} = 6\\sqrt{11}.\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between the vertices of the hyperbola is \\(\\boxed{6\\sqrt{11}}\\).",
